\chapter{Store}

The store is where the design stops being a pure document generator and becomes
a persistent polling system.  It has four jobs:
\begin{description}
\item[Configuration] locate the shared configuration file in a way that works
  both from the CLI and from PythonTeX,
\item[Placement] resolve the files a slide deck names relative to the
  deck's own directory, even when the deck is bound into a larger document,
\item[Registration] assign stable URL prefixes to questions and mark which
  of them the deck held in its last build, and
\item[Persistence] keep the questions in a file that is only ever replaced whole,
  so a half-written file never replaces a valid one, and the answers in a log
  beside it that is only ever appended to, so no write can undo another.
\end{description}

